#: ../../source/guides/devops/fingerprints.rst:3
msgid "Fingerprints and version discipline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fingerprints.rst:5
msgid ""
"Three repositories declare a hash of their own contents. Until this work,"
" **nothing computed it** — and a field nobody verifies is not a "
"fingerprint, it is a comment that looks like one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fingerprints.rst:9
msgid "The recipe, once"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fingerprints.rst:15
msgid ""
"The paths relative to the repository root, sorted in byte order; the "
"sha256 of each, in that order, as ``\"<hash>  <path>\"`` lines; and the "
"sha256 of that stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fingerprints.rst:18
msgid ""
"**The path is inside the hashed lines on purpose**: moving a file changes"
" the fingerprint as much as editing it. A grant naming ``tests/a.json`` "
"does not cover the same repository once that file is called "
"``tests/b.json``. The sort is ``LC_ALL=C`` so the answer does not depend "
"on the committer's locale — the one thing a fingerprint must never do is "
"differ between two people looking at the same tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fingerprints.rst:24
msgid ""
"Non-ASCII file names would need ``sha256sum``'s escaping rules pinned "
"down to stay reproducible. Both hooks already refuse them, so this says "
"so rather than pretending to handle a case nobody can currently create."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fingerprints.rst:29
msgid "A formats repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fingerprints.rst:31
msgid ""
"``info.validation_sha256`` in ``package.yaml`` covers **every file a "
"grant covers**, read from the repository's own ``validation/*.yaml`` — "
"not from ``freeports-validate collect``, because collecting resolves "
"methodology pages over the network and a fingerprint that cannot be "
"computed on a train is one the hook has to skip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fingerprints.rst:36
msgid ""
"When it moves, ``info.version`` must move too. Which component is the "
"author's choice: the change may be a correction or a whole new format, "
"and only they know which."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fingerprints.rst:39
msgid ""
"On ``dev`` the hook warns and **does not write the new fingerprint**. "
"Writing it would leave the manifest claiming that version X covers "
"content Y, which is a false statement — and the entire point of the field"
" is that it is not one."
msgstr ""

